  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Advisory for the East Africa Community</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the NDC Partnership has approached GGGI if we would be interested to support the EAC with TA with a fixed budget of 250,000 USD specifically focused on NDC implementation and Climate Finance. As with the previous NDC-P opportunity we know we can also indicate what we can&apos;t do for this amount they offer. So for example delivery 5 might be a bit enthusiastic without funding for (pre)feasibilities and workshops can be organised but travel budgets are (of course) excluded. Specific outputs/deliverables EAC overarching NDC road map 2021-206, and migration of the regional NDC Implementation Plan into the online platform. Bi -Annual regional peer to peer knowledge and learning exchange events Bi &#x2013;annual regional investors round table dialogues A regional capacity needs assessment report on climate financing and a capacity building plan. At least 4 regional NDC related programmes or project proposals/initiative funded Getting Burundi, South Sudan and Tanzania enrolling and engaging with the NDC Partnership Activities to achieve outputs/deliverables Revision of the 2018 EAC NDC Road Map based on the updated NDCs and the current contexts. Organizing regional climate change meetings to develop common climate change priorities and sharing best practices and lessons learnt. conduct EA regional surveys to get member state views on their NDCs implementation support needs and prioritization across the five years. Capacity needs assessments and coordinating appropriate capacity building support. Organizing donor/investor engagement workshops to showcase NDC investment opportunities. Identifying and mobilizing effective, innovative and appropriate financing for priority climate action in the EAC. Promoting available mechanisms to mobilize additional climate finance.</narrative>
  </description>
